description.narrative:
The proposed project will respond to urgent need to address unpredicted deterioration of human security of IDPs in protracted displacement in El Fasher, North Darfur, whose situations have been exacerbated by the political crisis of Sudan following the military coup of October 2021, UNAMID withdrawal and the high presence of militants in the region, intercommunal clashes, COVID-19 and the poor harvest in 2021 and 2022. 

The project aims to contribute to the sustainable peace and community stabilization by responding to neglected human security of the IDPs through supporting the return, resettlement and reintegration of IDPs in urban resettlement areas and rural return areas of El Fasher, North Darfur, in a manner that reduces tensions and contributes to peace building between IDPs, host communities, nomads and other affected communities. The project is intended to help create conditions conducive to sustainable solutions to the protracted displacement, through:
•	Gaining commitment to guiding principle of IDP return, resettlement and reintegration and securing their land rights;
•	Identifying, demarcating and registering land of the area of IDP resettlement in the target areas; 
•	Improving access to basic services and public infrastructure in the target areas; and
•	Diversifying the livelihood options and improving the self-resilience of the IDPs and host communities, particularly youth and women, through training on self-help reconstruction.
